  "dev_notes": [
   {
    "title": {
     "zh": "风格定调：沿用渔喵传说",
     "en": "Setting the look: borrowing from FishyTails"
    },
    "body": {
     "zh": "我一开始就定了方向：沿用我之前渔喵传说的 8bit 竖屏开罗风。游戏是 180×320 的像素画布，没有一张图片素材：每个人物都是 20×34 的参数化小人，按年龄、发型、服装、眼镜、拐杖拼出来，场景也全用代码绘制。",
     "en": "I set the direction on day one: reuse the 8-bit portrait Kairosoft style of my earlier game FishyTails. The game runs on a 180×320 pixel canvas with no image assets. Every person is a 20×34 sprite assembled from parameters (age, hairstyle, outfit, glasses, walking cane) and every scene is drawn in code."
    }
   },
   {
    "title": {
     "zh": "试玩驱动的角色与场景调整",
     "en": "Playtesting shaped the characters and scenes"
    },
    "body": {
     "zh": "试玩后我发现，秃头和啤酒肚用在女生身上不合适，改为按性别给出不同的衰老表现；我觉得场景单调、富豪家也该不一样，于是家分成五档，从农家土坯房到带喷泉花园的庄园，还加了新发型和便装；标题页也因为我觉得粗糙，重画成一条人生长街。",
     "en": "After playing, I flagged that baldness and a beer belly looked wrong on women, so aging now differs by gender. I found the scenes monotonous and said a rich family's home should look rich, so homes split into five tiers, from a mud-brick farmhouse to an estate with a fountain garden, with new hairstyles and casual outfits. I also called the title screen rough, and it became a street that walks through every stage of life."
    }
   },
   {
    "title": {
     "zh": "文字说什么，画面就是什么",
     "en": "If the text says it, the picture shows it"
    },
    "body": {
     "zh": "我反复抓到文字和立绘对不上：妖族化回原形人却没变狐狸、道侣飞升了还站在画面里。于是定下规则：文字出现「原形」就画九尾狐，离开故事的人也离开画面，隐藏路线不用现代场景。之后两轮模拟人生审查又修掉约 220 处矛盾。",
     "en": "I kept catching mismatches between text and sprites: a fox spirit \"returning to true form\" while still drawn as a human, a partner who had ascended still standing on stage. The fixes became rules: any year whose text mentions the true form draws the fox, anyone who leaves the story leaves the stage, and hidden routes never use modern scenes. Two audit rounds over simulated lives then caught about 220 more contradictions."
    }
   },
   {
    "title": {
     "zh": "命运胶囊：把一个天赋交给系统",
     "en": "The fate capsule: handing one talent to fate"
    },
    "body": {
     "zh": "原版是三个天赋全自选。我提出让系统随机定一个、玩家改不了，最后做成「一个天命＋两个自选」：扭蛋机先吐出一颗命运胶囊，四成概率开出诅咒，开到诅咒补偿 3 点属性。我又追问转世还能有什么好处，于是有了轮回殿永久升级和「前世因果」。",
     "en": "In the original game you pick all three talents. I suggested letting the system roll one that the player can't change. It became one fate talent plus two of your choice: the machine drops a fate capsule first, 40% of them hold a curse, and a curse pays back 3 extra stat points. When I asked what else reincarnation should give, that led to the Hall of Reincarnation upgrades and past-life karma."
    }
   },
   {
    "title": {
     "zh": "写得少一点，才不像 AI",
     "en": "Less writing, less AI flavour"
    },
    "body": {
     "zh": "我发现有些事件写得太满，比如海盗线红胡子的故事显得油腻，于是定下规则：每条事件不超过三行，只写发生了什么，细节一多「AI 味」就重。约 120 条长事件因此重写。加入同性恋情时也按我「不要太刻意」的想法，当作普通爱情来写。",
     "en": "I found some events overwritten; a pirate captain's farewell read as greasy. I set a rule: no event longer than three lines, just say what happened, because piling on detail is what makes text read as AI-written. About 120 long events were rewritten. When same-sex love was added, it followed my note to not make a big deal of it: it plays out like any other love story."
    }
   }
  ],
